# Stage 9 deliverables: 108 MB of DXF alone, regenerated by `python s9_export.py` in
# minutes, in a repo already carrying a 68 MB GeoPackage against GitHub's 100 MB limit.
# The schedules (CSV) and the report ARE committed - they are what anyone reads remotely.
W11a/dxf/
W11a/sewergems/
W11a/img/

# Terrain intermediates: raw numpy arrays of the filled DEM, flow accumulation and basin
# ids - 2.8 GB in a single file. They regenerate from terrain.py in minutes, and a 1.4 GB
# blob in git history is permanent even after deletion. The derived VECTORS (streams,
# basins, catchments) ARE committed - those are the answers, these are the workings.
W11b/run/terrain/*.npy
W11b/run/terrain/*.tif

# W11b design outputs. One reach layer alone is 104 MB, past GitHub's 100 MB HARD limit, so
# a push carrying it can never succeed. Every one of these regenerates from W11b/py in
# minutes. What IS committed is what someone reading remotely actually needs: the code, the
# docs, the CSV schedules and the KMZ - which is 0.7 MB and is the thing you open to judge
# the design.
W11b/shp/*.gpkg
W11b/shp/*.dbf
W11b/shp/*.shp
W11b/shp/*.shx
W11b/shp/*.prj
W11b/shp/*.cpg
W11b/run/**/*.gpkg
W11b/run/terrain/
